# Security rules

- Treat all IPC payloads as untrusted.
- No shell interpolation of URLs, filenames, or proxy strings.
- Cookies and secrets never go to logs or telemetry.
- Keep Tauri capabilities least-privilege.
- Reject path traversal and unexpected URL schemes.
- Do not commit `.env`, cookies, or local databases.
